cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  What Structured Pruning Actually Buys: Why Selection Criteria Stop
  Mattering
message: Please cite the paper if you use this artifact.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sau
    given-names: Priyadip
  - family-names: Das
    given-names: Debasis
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and analysis pipeline for a re-analysis of 3922
  structured-pruning runs across fully connected, convolutional and Transformer
  models, showing that the consumer-side repair dominates the selection
  criterion at deployable budgets, and giving an exact orthogonal decomposition
  that explains why.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - structured pruning
  - model compression
  - network pruning
  - least squares reconstruction
  - intrinsic dimension
